An illustrated scene from the classic children’s story titled "$title$".

Illustration Purpose:
Depict a recognizable moment, relationship, or setting from the story "$title$".
The scene must feel like it belongs only to this story — not a generic romantic or decorative image.

Style Guide:
- Imitate a page from European children’s picture books (1970s–1990s), like works by Shirley Hughes, Gyo Fujikawa, or Ladybird Books
- Use traditional media (watercolor, colored pencil, ink and wash)
- Include hand-drawn linework and paper texture to create a vintage, printed-book look

Character Focus:
- Must include at least one human character in the foreground (preferably two or more), and all characters must be either actual children or adults — no ambiguous age, chibi, or child-like adults
- Characters are the main subject — never overshadowed by scenery or props
- Show full or half-body with **historically appropriate clothing only**
- Faces must feature dot-like or oval eyes, rounded noses, and gentle, modest expressions
- **Strictly no modern accessories or items** (no backpacks, headphones, digital objects, etc.)

Composition:
- Characters must be centered and large enough to clearly show posture and expression
- Background (e.g., cottage, schoolhouse, garden) supports setting but remains secondary
- Scene must hint at a specific moment, object, or relationship from the story "$title$"
- Props are allowed only if historically accurate and subtle (e.g., baskets, books, flowers)

Mood and Tone:
- Soft, warm, nostalgic
- Designed for children ages 8–12 — quiet, human, comforting
- No cinematic drama, romantic tension, or fantasy atmosphere

Strictly Avoid:
- No anime/manga/manhwa styles
- No glossy rendering, shiny eyes/lips, or digital gradients
- No dramatic lighting or intense emotion
- No visible book text or formatting
- **No modern items or outfits of any kind**
- No stylized characters with ambiguous age — all characters must clearly appear as either children or adults
Output Goal:
A warm, human-centered, vintage illustration reflecting a clear moment from "$title$".
It should feel like a timeless picture book page — scanned from a beloved, well-read children’s book.